STEP 1: the non-GR sector depends on the metric ONLY through the scalar shat
   X0 = 1 - w^2 ?  True
   ln N |_O(ep)  = -shat/(1-w^2) ?  True
   A = a.a = [(grad s)^2 + (w.grad s)^2/(1-w^2)] with s=-shat/(1-w^2) ?  True
   ==> the LV sector is a functional of shat ALONE (any F(A), any auxiliary,
       and the TT carrier f(chi) Q^ij [a_i a_j]^TF - (1/2) Q^ij M Q_ij too,
       because a_mu itself depends on the metric only through shat).

STEP 2/3: linearised Bianchi identity  d_i G^{(1)0i} = 0  for static fields
   d_i G^{(1)0i} = 0   (identically zero for static h)

STEP 4: explicit linear solve, beta=lam=0, single Fourier mode k along z
   --- w = 0 (khronon at rest)
      rank(M) = 4  rank([M|b]) = 4
      Phi = 40*pi/9
      Psi = 40*pi/9
      Z_x = 0
      G_eff/G (coefficient of the Newtonian solution) = 10/9    [MOND-sector prediction 1/(1-alpha/2) = -2/(alpha - 2) ]
      shat on-shell = 40*pi/9    (shat = 0  =>  the entire non-GR stress vanishes)
   --- w != 0 (boosted khronon), w=(1/7,0,1/3)
      rank(M) = 5  rank([M|b]) = 5
      Phi = 4*pi
      Psi = 4*pi
      Z_x = 0
      G_eff/G (coefficient of the Newtonian solution) = 1    [MOND-sector prediction 1/(1-alpha/2) = -2/(alpha - 2) ]
      shat on-shell = 0    (shat = 0  =>  the entire non-GR stress vanishes)
   --- w != 0 symbolic direction, wx=0
      rank(M) = 5  rank([M|b]) = 5
      Phi = 4*pi
      Psi = 4*pi
      Z_x = 0
      G_eff/G (coefficient of the Newtonian solution) = 1    [MOND-sector prediction 1/(1-alpha/2) = -2/(alpha - 2) ]
      shat on-shell = 0    (shat = 0  =>  the entire non-GR stress vanishes)

CONCLUSION: at beta = lam = 0 the boosted-khronon static solution is EXACTLY GR:
  alpha_1 = alpha_2 = 0, gamma = 1, G_eff = G -- and the MOND modification is GONE.
  At w = 0 exactly, MOND is present (G_eff = G/(1-alpha/2)).  Discontinuous limit.
